Ah, I see! You want a clean, dedicated expandable subsection inside the card, like a mini-dropdown that pushes the content down when you click it.
We can achieve this beautifully using Material UI's Collapse component. It creates a sleek animation that slides open to reveal the full description.
Here is how to build that dedicated subsection:
### 1. Update your Imports
First, scroll to the very top of your file and make sure you add Collapse to your @mui/material imports:
```javascript
import {
  // ... your other imports ...
  Collapse
} from "@mui/material";

```
### 2. Replace the Description Grid Item
Scroll back down to your **View Details Modal**. Find the <Grid item xs={12}> that contains the Description (inside SECTION 1: VOUCHER ORIGIN DETAILS) and replace it with this clean, expandable subsection:
```javascript
                        {/* --- EXPANDABLE SUBSECTION FOR DESCRIPTION --- */}
                        <Grid item xs={12}>
                          {/* A dashed line to separate it as a distinct subsection */}
                          <Box sx={{ borderTop: '1px dashed #cbd5e1', pt: 1.5, mt: 1 }}>
                            
                            {/* The Clickable Header */}
                            <Box 
                              onClick={() => setIsDescExpanded(!isDescExpanded)}
                              sx={{ 
                                display: 'flex', 
                                alignItems: 'center', 
                                justifyContent: 'space-between', 
                                cursor: 'pointer',
                                '&:hover': { opacity: 0.8 } // Small hover effect for UX
                              }}
                            >
                              <Typography variant="subtitle2" color="primary.main" fontWeight="bold">
                                View Voucher Description
                              </Typography>
                              <Typography variant="caption" color="primary.main" fontWeight="bold">
                                {isDescExpanded ? "Close ▲" : "Expand ▼"}
                              </Typography>
                            </Box>

                            {/* The Animated Dropdown Content */}
                            <Collapse in={isDescExpanded}>
                              <Box sx={{ 
                                mt: 1.5, 
                                backgroundColor: '#ffffff', 
                                border: '1px solid #cbd5e1', 
                                borderRadius: 1, 
                                p: 1.5 
                              }}>
                                <Typography variant="body2" color="text.primary" sx={{ whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
                                  {vidDetails.DESCRIPTION || "No description provided."}
                                </Typography>
                              </Box>
                            </Collapse>
                            
                          </Box>
                        </Grid>

```
### Why this looks incredibly professional:
 * **Distinct UI Area:** The dashed line visually separates the standard stats from the long-form text.
 * **Animated Reveal:** The Collapse component automatically calculates the height of your 500-word description and smoothly slides it open and closed.
 * **Zero Clutter:** When closed, it takes up almost no space, keeping your modal looking perfectly balanced.
